  "source": {
    "key": "bls-detail-bag",
    "title": "BLS DETAIL BAG",
    "version_label": "REV 2020",
    "file_name": "bls_detail_bag_medical_inventory.pdf",
    "sha256": "7dba064af14b43d107d4c5d00fae6341346ba2167a5f52db5611983b542cbbc4",
    "pages": 1,
    "columns": [
      "ITEM",
      "(quantity; no heading is printed)"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "Transcribed from the one-page PDF bls_detail_bag_medical_inventory.pdf (sha256 above). Two printed columns of ITEM and one unlabeled quantity cell each; the left column is read top to bottom, then the right column.",
      "Left column: FRONT POUCH, LEFT SIDE (6), RIGHT SIDE (5), POUCH 4, POUCH 3, POUCH 2. Right column: COMPARTMENT 1, MAIN COMPARTMENT. The (6) and (5) are part of the printed headings and are kept in the section labels; the sheet does not say what they mean.",
      "The sheet prints one quantity per item and no \"Fill if <\" and no NEED column. The quantity is the par (min_text / min_qty / min_unit); the member types what is needed. \"1 BOX\" is kept exactly as printed (min_unit box).",
      "source_label is the printed text including its capital letters and its misspellings (TRAMUA SHEARS, ORAL GLUCTOSE, TYVEX SLEEVES, STETHESCOPE, BAND AIDES, MADDETT). label corrects only an obvious spelling of the same product; the misspelled form is kept as a search term.",
      "Two empty table rows (under ADULT PADS and under BURN GEL 4X4) carry no text and no number."
    ],
    "printed_header": "BLS DETAIL BAG REV 2020",
    "review_notes": [
      "\"LEFT SIDE (6)\" and \"RIGHT SIDE (5)\" print a number in brackets that is not a count of the rows under them (4 and 4). It may be a pouch number. Kept in the printed heading.",
      "\"OPAS 2 ADULT\", \"OPAS 1 CHILD\" and \"OPAS 1 INF\" print no OPA sizes; the quantities 2, 1 and 1 equal the numbers in the labels."
    ]
  },
